Thanks!  I think that's a bit of information a lot of us were missing,
as it's not mentioned in any spoiler I've seen.  I'm going to
elaborate, for anybody else who might have been as curious as I as to
how this works:

Every game turn (as in when the turncount increments), there is a 1/15
chance that, if you are wielding or wearing the Amulet, it will feel
warm if you are near any magic portal.

The message is based on the distance to the portal, using Nethack's
usual sum-of-squares distance calculation:

<=   9 (radius 3 squares)  = "The Amulet of Yendor feels hot!"
<=  64 (radius 8 squares)  = "The Amulet of Yendor feels very warm."
<= 144 (radius 12 squares) = "The Amulet of Yendor feels warm."
Farther away and you get no message.

Especially if you're fast/very fast, it wouldn't be hard at all to
stumble into the portal on Water before triggering one of these, and
probably quite easy to do so before triggering a "hot!" message.

It strikes me as a wholly unreliable method of determining that
you're about to step on the portal so you can stop and prepare for
Astral.

